diff -ruN orig/debian/changelog new/debian/changelog
--- a/debian/changelog	2026-11-05 17:48:02.701373575 -0800
+++ b/debian/changelog	2026-11-05 17:51:00.776338358 -0800
@@ -1,3 +1,21 @@
+pve-cluster (9.1.7+supermox3) trixie; urgency=medium
+
+  * debian: setup_single_node_cluster now does nothing when the package is being
+    built. It used to write /etc/corosync/corosync.conf from `hostname` and
+    `hostname -I`, which inside a build chroot are the *build machine's* name
+    and address: the PC ISO booted with a config naming localhost.localdomain
+    and corosync died parsing that bindnet address, so /etc/pve stayed read-only
+    and pve-cluster could not seed storage.cfg. The script now compares the
+    dev:inode of / with that of /proc/1/root/. and returns when they differ, so
+    an image never carries an identity that no node will ever have. supermox-ve
+    ships init.d/supermox-corosync, which writes the single-node config from the
+    booting node's own hostname and non-loopback address before corosync starts,
+    and rewrites it when the address or the hostname changed; a real multi-node
+    cluster config is never touched. Installing on a booted node still works as
+    before.
+
+ -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 17:50:40 -0800
+
 pve-cluster (9.1.7+supermox2) trixie; urgency=medium
 
   * debian: init.d/pve-cluster seeds /etc/pve/storage.cfg. pmxcfs creates that
